/*
:name: concat_tuple_lanes
:type: equiv
:verilog_top: concat_tuple_lanes.top
:pyrope_top: top
*/

// FAILS TODAY, DELIBERATELY UNTAGGED. `prp-equiv-concat_tuple_lanes`,
// `prp-statematch-concat_tuple_lanes` and `prp-v2prp2v-concat_tuple_lanes` are
// ordinary targets and they are RED — no `fixme` tag hides them, because the
// point of this pair is to be the thing that is fixed. Do not tag it; fix it.
//
// The two DOCUMENTED concat lane spellings that reach a bundle's fields. Both
// hard-error today, so this pair does not even get as far as an equivalence
// check — it is the minimal repro for that, and the sibling
// concat_bundle_lanes pair is the green one that covers everything around it.
//
//   zt   `concat(p, c)` — a TUPLE lane. docs/pyrope/10-internals.md: "A tuple
//        lane expands to its fields in declaration order (field 0 most
//        significant), provided every field has a declared type." Reports
//        `concat-untyped-lane: concat lane `p` has no declared bit width`.
//
//   zd   `concat(p.hi, p.lo, c)` — DOTTED field lanes. Each field IS declared
//        (`hi:u4`, `lo:s3`), but a dotted read lowers through a compiler temp
//        (`store %z_0 = p.hi`), and the temp carries no declared type, so the
//        lane check sees `concat lane `%z_0` has no declared bit width`.
//
// Where it breaks: `uPass_runner::check_concat_lanes` /
// `concat_lane_declared_bits` (upass/runner/upass_runner.cpp) resolve a lane
// only through `concat_result_bits_` and `decl_facts::lookup` on the lane's own
// name — neither a tuple's fields nor a copy of a declared name. The check runs
// on the DISPATCH path, so it fires before anything downstream can help:
// `uPass_constprop::process_concat` already carries a tuple-splice arm (the
// `is_tuple` branch, positional fields only) and it is UNREACHABLE today, and
// `upass.tolg::lower_concat` never sees the node either.
//
// Both outputs are the same nine bits, so the golden states one layout twice —
// which is also the claim that a tuple lane and its hand-spliced fields must
// agree.
pub comb top(p:(hi:u4, lo:s3), c:u2) -> (zt:u9, zd:u9) {
  zt = concat(p, c)            // tuple lane: hi (field 0) in the high bits
  zd = concat(p.hi, p.lo, c)   // the same layout, spliced by hand
}
